apprecorder itself is MIT. It links third-party libraries with their own terms,
and one of them places an obligation on anyone distributing a BINARY:

  libmp3lame (vendor/lame/)   LGPL-2.0-or-later
      Statically linked. LGPL section 6 requires that a recipient be able to
      relink the work with a modified version of the library, so a binary
      release must ship either the object files or this source tree, together
      with vendor/lame/COPYING and a visible notice. This obligation attaches
      to the release, not to apprecorder's own licence.

  libogg  (vendor/ogg/)       BSD-3-Clause  -- reproduce the notice
  libopus (vendor/opus/)      BSD-3-Clause  -- reproduce the notice
  jsmn    (vendor/jsmn/)      MIT           -- reproduce the notice

See docs/licensing.md for the release checklist.
